        "problem": "$4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})\\operatorname{csc}\u2061({140}^{\u2218})=$",
        "worked_solution": "First, let's recall the double-angle formula for sine: \n\n$$\n2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061x\\operatorname{cos}\u2061x=\\operatorname{sin}\u20612x\n$$\n\nSubstituting $x={70}^{\u2218}$ into the above, we get\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({70}^{\u2218}) & =\\operatorname{sin}\u2061(2\\cdot {70}^{\u2218})=\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({140}^{\u2218})\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nNow, we can rewrite the given expression using the above, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})\\operatorname{csc}\u2061({140}^{\u2218}) & =2\\cdot [2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})\\operatorname{cos}\u2061({70}^{\u2218})]\\operatorname{csc}\u2061({140}^{\u2218}) \\\\  & =2\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({140}^{\u2218})\\cdot \\frac{1}{\\operatorname{sin}\u2061({140}^{\u2218})} \\\\  & =2.\\end{aligned}\n$$",
